      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. PURE SUBSTANCE"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "A pure substance consists of a single type of substance with a fixed chemical composition and distinct properties.",
        "Homogeneous mixtures have a uniform composition throughout, whereas heterogeneous mixtures contain physically distinct parts.",
        "A solution is a homogeneous mixture of two or more substances consisting of a solute dissolved in a solvent.",
        "Colloids are heterogeneous mixtures where particle sizes are large enough to scatter light (Tyndall Effect) but small enough to remain suspended.",
        "Physical changes involve changes in physical properties without forming new substances, while chemical changes result in the formation of new chemical substances."
      ],
      "id": "q2htb8p"
    },
