    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Alloys (e.g., Brass = 30% Zinc + 70% Copper) are homogeneous mixtures that cannot be separated by physical methods.",
        "Tincture of iodine contains iodine as the solute and alcohol as the solvent, a common SSC objective question.",
        "Milk, blood, and fog are classic examples of colloids, whereas salt in water is a true solution.",
        "Rusting of iron and burning of candle wax involve chemical changes, while melting of ice is purely physical."
      ],
